    <statement><p>Find the parametric equations for the tangent line to the curve 
<me>x =
    t^{3} - 1, y = t^{3} + 1, z = t^{2}</me>
 at the
    point (26, 28, 9). Use
    the variable t for your parameter.</p>
<p><m>x =</m><fillin characters="25" name="AnSwEr0001"/>,</p>
<p><m>y =</m><fillin characters="25" name="AnSwEr0002"/>,</p>
<p><m>z =</m><fillin characters="25" name="AnSwEr0003"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>26+t\cdot 3\cdot 9</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>28+t\cdot 3\cdot 9</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>9+t\cdot 2\cdot 3</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
